#
# Hourly cadence, per ADR-0076 §Abnahme ("stündliche Sonde je Seite").
#
# One hour is also the measured ``default_x509_svid_ttl``, which means
# the sampling interval and the quantity being sampled are the same
# order of magnitude. That is a real limit and it is stated rather than
# papered over: the series can establish *that* the expiry moves, and it
# cannot count how many times it moved between two samples. The judge's
# Z2 tolerance is TTL + one interval for exactly this reason.
#
# A reboot inside the window costs the sample that was due while the node
# was down, and nothing here recovers it. ``OnBootSec=3min`` starts the
# series again three minutes after the node comes back; the hour that was
# missed stays missed.
#
# This file previously carried ``Persistent=true`` with a comment
# claiming it caught that case up. It does not: *"Note that this setting
# only has an effect on timers configured with OnCalendar="*
# (``man systemd.timer``, verified against systemd 258 on 2026-09-23).
# The behaviour was fine — ``OnBootSec=`` was doing the work — but the
# assurance was false, and a false assurance in a comment about an
# instrument is the exact shape of defect this whole acceptance exists
# to answer, in miniature. The setting is gone rather than paired with
# an ``OnCalendar=``, because even with one it would only add a sample
# stamped *now*, which is what ``OnBootSec=`` already produces. It would
# not fill the gap in the series.
#
# The gap is not hidden either way: the judge reports a stretch without
# samples as an unexplained coverage gap and the window comes out
# UNKNOWN. That is the correct answer about an hour nobody watched, and
# it is better than a setting that looks like it prevented one.
[Unit]
Description=Wakir ADR-0076 acceptance sample (%i side, hourly)
Documentation=https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/blob/main/docs/test-plans/adr-0076-seven-day-acceptance-window.md

[Timer]
OnBootSec=3min
OnUnitActiveSec=1h
RandomizedDelaySec=60s
Unit=wakir-substrate-acceptance-probe@%i.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
